  "id": "gene-mosaicism",
  "term": "gene mosaicism",
  "definition": "In this fragile X context, gene mosaicism means that one person has a mix of cells with different versions of the FMR1 gene, such as some cells with a methylated full mutation and others with a smaller unmethylated premutation. This mixed pattern has been linked with better cognitive functioning than having only the full mutation.",
